{{also|Feminist}}
==English==

===Etymology===
First recorded in English 1852. Ultimately from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|fēminīnus}}, from {{m|la|fēmina||woman}}. See also {{term|feminine|lang=en}}, {{term|feminism|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈfɛmənɪst/|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Relating to or in accordance with [[feminism]].
#* {{quote-book
  | date = 2000-05-01
  | author = {{w|bell hooks}}
  | title = {{w|Feminist Theory: From Margin to Center}}
  | edition = 2nd
  | page = xi
  | pageurl = http://books.google.com/books?id=uvIQbop4cdsC&pg=PR11
  | passage = '''Feminist''' struggle takes place anytime anywhere any female or male resists sexism, sexist exploitation, and oppression.
}}

